WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.010
- [Narrator] Middle ground
is a social experiment

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:02.850
that brings humans

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.580
with opposing beliefs
or experiences together.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.920
Remember to seek out
experts and to be critical

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.200
of your own biases while
forming an opinion.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.690
Please see the humanity
in each participant,

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.033
and as always, we encourage empathy.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:16.747
(dramatic music)

00:00:16.747 --> 00:00:17.827
- (news broadcast) He hasn't prepared.

00:00:17.827 --> 00:00:20.317
- (news broadcast) Russia
invading is (beep) psychotic.

00:00:20.317 --> 00:00:23.681
(Putin speaking Russian)

00:00:23.681 --> 00:00:26.931
(multi media extracts)

00:00:28.569 --> 00:00:31.819
(dramatic title music)

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.500
- Please raise your hand

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.243
if you agree with the prompt,

00:00:46.147 --> 00:00:49.500
"I am proud of my country."

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.946
Three, two, one.

00:00:51.946 --> 00:00:55.440
(computer beeps)

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.530
- All that Ukraine is doing now,

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.950
we are defending and we defend very well.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.194
Also, I'm proud of my president

00:01:04.194 --> 00:01:06.120
who didn't leave the country.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:09.690
And also I'm proud of all the Ukrainians

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.880
who are really connected.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.340
- I've never had these like

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:18.120
unrealistically good
perceptions about my country

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.920
because my, personally,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.480
my family had a situation
when we all suffered

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.040
because of corruption.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:30.780
That's, was and is a
big problem in Ukraine,

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.750
but this situation definitely made me

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.870
feel very proud of Ukrainian people.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:41.430
- So I'm really interested
in Sergei opinion.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:42.930
- I can explain myself.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.240
I distinguish the state and the country.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.210
For me, the state is waging the war

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:52.530
and the country tries
to show the best in it

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.240
for tens of thousands of people

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.280
who come out to the streets of Moscow,

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.020
St Petersburg and other cities,

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.420
knowing for sure that they will be jailed.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.920
Some of them are badly beaten up.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.510
Some of them jailed for years.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.970
The risks they're taking are enormous

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:08.340
and they know well they're doing it

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.650
without hope of changing anything.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.450
But they're doing it for the sake

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:15.000
of showing important symbols

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.190
that not everyone agrees with the war.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:20.100
And I actually think
most of Russians disagree

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:20.933
with the war.

00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:23.310
The problem is that they are frightened,

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.690
they are isolated,

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:26.100
they're being threatened.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:29.820
And that makes me proud to the extent

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:34.820
that these dissident
movement is totally hopeless.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:38.010
but nevertheless, people
are choosing this.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.330
- Thank you for explanation.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.370
It means a lot.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.260
In your opinion, I will agree.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:47.340
So I will too support people in Russia

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:50.070
who really are against the war

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.620
and against of everything happening

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.543
who has like clear mind.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:57.720
I support them too.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:58.988
Thank you.

00:02:58.988 --> 00:03:01.020
- Can the disagreers unmute themselves

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:03.930
and join the conversation please?

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:07.410
- Yeah, I just, I completely
agree with Sergei.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:10.200
I am not proud of the government.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.760
I'm not proud of the government's actions.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:15.330
But I am proud of people who are here

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.180
and who I know are good Russian people

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:21.660
and who I hope are the
future of this country.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:24.690
- No matter what happened this year,

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:26.220
if you ask me the same question,

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.590
let's say one year ago or five years ago,

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.930
I would have the same answer.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:32.970
I am not proud of my country.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:37.620
It never cared about regular people much.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:41.250
When I see at what kind
of lives people have here

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.190
especially after traveling
to a few other countries,

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:48.270
I simply cannot say that
I'm proud of my country.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.880
Seeing that my babushka,

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:53.884
my grandmother is having a pension

00:03:53.884 --> 00:03:57.990
that is lower that minimal wage

00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:01.860
and minimal possible
amount of money to survive.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:06.060
Of course, we have a lot
of good sides of Russia,

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.010
like the guys say, people.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.520
But talking about do
I like it here or not,

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:12.945
about the state?

00:04:12.945 --> 00:04:14.580
No, not at all.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.770
- It would be irresponsible

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:20.520
for the US to get more involved.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.733
Three, two, one.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:31.460
- In 1994, Ukraine gave all
their weapon, nuclear weapon

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.020
from their territory.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:42.020
That was a document between
United States and also Russia.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:45.960
They needed guarantee to be defended.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:49.140
If every, if something
will happen like this.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.640
Now it happened,

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:55.640
but Ukraine still asks all the countries

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:56.490
for the weapon.

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:58.230
If we have weapon to defense,

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:01.470
if there are any invaders coming,

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:03.870
we could defense in a proper way.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.027
- United States cannot be a bystander.

00:05:06.027 --> 00:05:08.220
And it is not a bystander,

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:13.220
by supporting the Ukraine,
the Ukrainian resistance.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:17.280
And of course it would
be irresponsible not

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.860
to be involved, for the United States,

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:22.650
particularly given what
has already happened.

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:27.420
- I understand why NATO soldiers
are still not in Ukraine

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:31.140
because that can trigger

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:34.050
a very dangerous button there in Russia.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.090
So I understand why no one wants

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:39.270
to take this kind of risks.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.960
When we know one person, Vladimir Putin,

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:44.310
who can press the button

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:47.190
and everyone on this
planet is going to die.

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:50.640
But I agree that it would be irresponsible

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:54.750
to just leave things as they are.

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.330
- I'm gonna just throw a
follow up question in here.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:01.383
Is anyone here concerned about
nuclear weapons being used?

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:06.480
- I'm not sure.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:11.480
I think that there's this
power of Putin and his button.

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:17.100
I think it's looks like more than it is.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.340
We see that Ukrainian
soldiers are doing their best.

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:24.180
They are excellent in their job

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:27.090
but there is a lack of weapon.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:29.460
- I think it should be not only weapons,

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:31.620
but also humanitarian help,

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.170
like given food to the regions

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:37.260
who are under attack
currently or occupied.

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:40.740
So yes, soldiers, it is super risky

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:43.560
because it will be seen as an act of war

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:45.480
from other countries towards Russia.

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:48.300
But it should be, should
not be only weapons.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.470
It should be something

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.330
for the people who live there as well.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:52.890
- In occupied territories

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:56.910
Russians do not let
humanitarian help to get in.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:59.850
There is a lot of humanitarian help,

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:03.120
but they do not let them in.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:05.490
They are killing civil people.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:07.620
They're killing volunteers.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:11.550
Just that person who wants to help.

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:14.640
I think only like a weapon

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:17.880
and only hard decisions could help.

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:20.080
- I'm concerned, concerned about

00:07:21.404 --> 00:07:24.540
Putin threatening the world with nuclears,

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.900
because we already seen Russian military

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:30.650
being in Zaporizhzhia and Chernobyl

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:33.180
which was very dangerous situation.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.190
I believe that it can be just threatening,

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:37.500
just act to scare us.

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:41.190
But also months before the war started

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:43.830
Putin kind of tried to scare the world

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:46.440
that he will start the war,

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.400
but promised he wouldn't,
and he still started.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:54.270
- My life has changed since the war began.

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:57.546
Three, two, one.

00:07:57.546 --> 00:08:00.296
(computer beeps)

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:06.210
- Actually my life and
I think lives of all,

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:09.870
almost all Ukrainians
are not just changed,

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:11.730
they are crashed.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:14.163
On the February 24th,

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:20.120
I wake up from the lightening and

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:23.850
from hearing the sounds of bombs.

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.703
I had about, I dunno,

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:29.970
one hour

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:34.620
to gather my all things that I need.

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:39.620
And now I really need to start my new life

00:08:39.673 --> 00:08:41.310
from the beginning.

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:43.170
- I had to leave Ukraine too.

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:46.440
The fact that I cannot just come back home

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.270
and I also had to pack very fast.

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:50.520
I, to just a little stuff.

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:53.010
I just wanna come home and hug my parents.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:55.470
I want to make my parents leave Ukraine

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:57.060
and they don't want to leave.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:58.410
I'm worried about them.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:02.910
I don't think any Ukrainian
now has the same life.

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:05.190
- Everything pales in comparison

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:08.530
with what Ukrainians have to go through

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:11.850
and how their lives have changed.

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:15.480
However, many people who hail from Russia

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:17.790
had their whole life changed as well,

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:18.780
in a different way.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.810
As a lawyer, I was doing
cases against Russia

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:24.333
with, in the European
Court of Human Rights.

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:27.120
And as a direct consequence of the war,

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:30.060
Russia was expelled from
the Council of Europe

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:32.070
and the whole litigation

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:34.830
in the European Court of Human
Rights is now meaningless.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:37.440
A lot of people, including
myself, have to leave Russia.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:39.510
For me, it was important to leave

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:44.070
because I don't want to pay
a cent in taxes in Russia.

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:46.800
It's a small thing, but
it is important thing.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:49.950
- First of all my mother lost her job

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:51.990
because she was working
for international company

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:56.190
and they are not able to
transfer money right now

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:57.630
to Russia due to sanctions.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:01.140
But I was not able to find a lot of meds

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:05.490
that I need and I had
to order some of them.

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:07.710
And while they were coming here,

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.030
I had to live without them.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:10.770
My girlfriend, she's American,

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:13.470
and she used to help me to pay for them.

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:14.970
Now she can't

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:18.362
because there's no way she
can transfer money here.

00:10:18.362 --> 00:10:21.060
And I, myself, I can't afford them.

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:23.703
- I think that Ukrainians,

00:10:23.703 --> 00:10:27.540
even who leave their country,

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:29.580
I don't think they feel safe.

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:34.580
We know examples when Russians
beat bartender in a bar

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:38.580
because he was on the Ukrainian.

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:43.580
We also saw the rally that
supports the war, in Berlin.

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:46.680
- We need to find a place where to stay.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:50.265
We have these thoughts,
not like what to do today.

00:10:50.265 --> 00:10:51.990
We need to think, where do we sleep?

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:52.823
What do we eat?

00:10:52.823 --> 00:10:53.850
How do we make money?

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:55.710
A lot of people came without documents

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:59.010
and they cannot even get
international passport

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:00.780
or even Ukrainian passport

00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:03.150
because embassy doesn't give it.

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:07.110
A very close friend
tried to escape Ukraine,

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:08.490
but through Russian border.

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:11.520
And they would have to go
through a lot of block post.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.200
One Russian soldier asked him

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:17.430
to give his sneakers to the soldier.

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:20.850
- And that's actually why
the Russian army is losing

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:22.890
because if the army starts marauding,

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:26.130
if the army starts stealing, it's done.

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:28.590
You never win when you're
stealing from the locals.

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:32.640
- We all had this illusion that we live

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:35.610
in the new age, in the new world

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:39.330
where human rights are above everything.

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:42.780
And now we just see that
this is not how it is,

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:47.780
and wars are not the
leftovers from past century.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.510
It can still happen.

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:55.170
And this, just as a phenomenon,

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:57.510
makes me feel very unsafe.

00:11:57.510 --> 00:12:00.360
- I live in St Petersburg city.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:04.470
And since the very beginning of the war,

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:07.710
I had some concerns
about my personal safety

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:11.100
in terms of getting trouble
with laws and with police.

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:13.110
I've joined quite a few protests.

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:17.670
So I also filmed it and
made videos on my YouTube

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.350
and TikTok channels.

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:23.820
And I was expecting
that I would face a risk

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:26.280
of getting fined or
getting some jail time.

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:30.330
And I kind of accepted that small risk.

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:32.794
Eventually I will leave Russia.

00:12:32.794 --> 00:12:36.300
I came back to Russia two years ago

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:38.940
and I planned to leave Russia in like one

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:41.040
or two years from now.

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:43.320
And perhaps I'll have to leave earlier

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:44.970
but I'm not leaving ASAP.

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:46.590
- And I'm actually also
from St Petersburg.

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:47.610
I think there are two problems.

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:49.740
One, when you have problems with law

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:51.870
then you will not be allowed to leave.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:52.950
It will be too late.

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:55.980
And second, in one or
two years, in my opinion

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:58.230
there will be no opportunity
to leave altogether.

00:12:58.230 --> 00:12:59.670
The border will be closed.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:02.340
Frankly, if you really think about leaving

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:04.680
and you have opportunity to do that,

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.357
do it yesterday.

00:13:06.357 --> 00:13:10.050
- I am immune to propaganda.

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:13.833
Three, two, one.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:21.800
- The trick that's
propaganda uses very often,

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:26.730
sometimes they do not even
show the actual narrative

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:29.640
and try to make people believe that.

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:34.640
Sometimes they just start
telling many different stories

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:39.780
to create this impression

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:42.900
that people cannot trust anyone.

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:46.086
And this is a very
powerful trick, I think.

00:13:46.086 --> 00:13:48.870
- I tend to compare
propaganda to junk food.

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:50.910
It's easy to access.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:52.380
It's easy to consume.

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:54.540
It makes you happy for a while.

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:57.510
And of course you are obsessive with it.

00:13:57.510 --> 00:13:59.850
It kills doubt in people.

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:03.180
It gives them clear road view,

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:05.040
which is very easy to live with.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:09.060
Doubt, which should exist for
research, for understanding,

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:11.880
is also very difficult thing to live with.

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:14.700
So paradoxically, people
who consume propaganda

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:16.950
are happy to keep consuming it,

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:18.390
like with junk food.

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:21.210
And that's why I don't think I'm immune,

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.860
as well as I'm not immune
to junk food unfortunately.

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:27.450
- Julia, Niki and Sergei, is it true

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:32.450
that in Russia all the independent
TV channels were closed?

00:14:32.786 --> 00:14:34.255
- Now, yes.

00:14:34.255 --> 00:14:37.080
Now there are no independent
TV channels at all.

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.730
And there are no independent newspapers.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:41.760
The only independent
journalists left in Russia

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:43.473
are actually foreign correspondents.

00:14:43.473 --> 00:14:45.657
And there are few and fewer of them.

00:14:45.657 --> 00:14:47.550
- The only way to go for something

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:50.850
that's not like from the
state, is to go online.

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:52.980
And even then you have
to be super careful.

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:54.300
- And use VPN, yes.

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:59.100
There are some medias
that were not only closed.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:00.540
They were banned online.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:03.930
- Yeah, I have a friend in
Russia, when everything started

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:07.290
she just posted her like champagne life.

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:10.297
You know, I like ask her,

00:15:10.297 --> 00:15:13.331
"Why you don't post anything

00:15:13.331 --> 00:15:15.000
on your social media?"

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.550
And she said, "I'm just a small person.

00:15:17.550 --> 00:15:18.600
What can I do?"

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:23.600
And that is like the worst
answer that can be for me.

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.940
'Cause these two months showed

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:30.333
that people are doing something like,

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:35.970
even in social media when
you say your opinion,

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:38.850
you like make seen your voice.

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:40.980
It influences the situation.

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:44.010
It can influence on bigger organization

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:48.180
when people raise and say something.

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:53.180
- A war between Ukraine
and Russia was inevitable.

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:57.003
Three, two, one.

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:02.207
- There was no underlying
reason for the war.

00:16:02.207 --> 00:16:06.150
It was started by actually,
basically one person.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.253
- Yes.

00:16:07.253 --> 00:16:10.632
The fact that that person
met no resistance for years-

00:16:10.632 --> 00:16:12.217
- I disagree that there was no resistance.

00:16:12.217 --> 00:16:14.280
There are tens of thousands of people

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.570
who spent time in jail,

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:18.994
who are in jail right now,
for daring to protest.

00:16:18.994 --> 00:16:21.300
There have been journalists killed

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:24.210
who tried to come out with the truth.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:27.780
There have been activists
pushed out of the country

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:31.530
or detained, or beaten,
or actually murdered.

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.000
So the resistance was there.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:35.100
Unfortunately it was not successful.

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:37.387
- Like my grandparents, they are like,

00:16:37.387 --> 00:16:39.600
"Yes, it's good that Russia is there,"

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:41.700
but they don't know
what's actually happening.

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:43.410
And they only watch TV.

00:16:43.410 --> 00:16:46.350
They don't browse through the internet

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:48.150
because they think that internet is bad

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:50.790
and only misinformation happens there.

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:55.620
I think if we show actual
facts to Russian people,

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.280
to all of the Russian people,

00:16:57.280 --> 00:17:01.320
there will be a lot less
people who agree with this.

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:03.180
- You know, it's really easy to tell

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:07.650
that somebody do not
believe what's happening,

00:17:07.650 --> 00:17:10.140
but if they really do not believe

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:11.370
they can come,

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:12.870
they can come to the border.

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:14.520
Why do not they do that?

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:16.567
'Cause it's so easy to tell,

00:17:16.567 --> 00:17:18.113
"I don't believe it."

00:17:18.113 --> 00:17:19.465
- No, no, no.

00:17:19.465 --> 00:17:22.080
- It's so easy to tell
that everything is false

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:26.490
but why shouldn't they
go and see by their eyes?

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:28.470
They don't wanna do that.

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:32.910
- I feel there will be
a winner in this war.

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:36.213
Three, two, one.

00:17:37.489 --> 00:17:39.930
(computer beeps)

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:43.230
- For me, this is not a war
between Russia and Ukraine.

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:47.820
The actual war is between
dictatorship and freedom.

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:50.250
That's actually why
Putin attacked Ukraine,

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:51.300
I think in a nutshell.

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:55.440
He detests democracy,
rights, and liberties.

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:58.860
And I'm convinced that democracy, rights,

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:00.720
liberties and freedoms will prevail.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:02.730
And paradoxically, and ironically,

00:18:02.730 --> 00:18:06.420
that is perhaps the
positive outcome of this war

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:11.340
because this war reminded those countries

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:14.370
which are free, what they should value.

00:18:14.370 --> 00:18:16.920
That they should value,
not the natural gas flowing

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:17.753
from Russia.

00:18:17.753 --> 00:18:20.040
They should value the
liberties that they have,

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:21.600
security that they have.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.850
And because of Ukraine, they're reminded

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:25.860
that it's so easy to lose all of this,

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:27.540
unless you stick to your principles

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:29.610
and to your values and
they're able to defend them.

00:18:29.610 --> 00:18:33.840
That's why I'm pretty
optimistic that in the end

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.930
it will be a great reawakening
for those countries

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:39.900
which are free and why
they should stick together,

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:44.900
protect themselves and push
the totalitarian countries

00:18:45.510 --> 00:18:46.343
to the brink.

00:18:46.343 --> 00:18:51.343
- I really hope that freedom will win.

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:56.340
- Ukrainians and Russian
people, just normal people,

00:18:56.340 --> 00:18:58.290
they will lose from both sides.

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:00.780
But talking about bigger
things, there will be like,

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:03.090
it's not about Russia and Ukraine.

00:19:03.090 --> 00:19:04.830
It's about totally bigger things.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:07.200
- Pretty sure I'm gonna sound very basic

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:08.430
but I'm gonna say it.

00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:11.160
No one wins in wars.

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:14.910
It's the matter of who has more damage,

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:19.910
and both sides will be damaged

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:23.430
and are being damaged already.

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:25.320
And I think

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:28.470
that Russia's damage is
going to be more long term

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:32.790
because this isolation will not stop.

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:37.790
If in some miraculous way,
the war stops tomorrow,

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:42.060
this is not going to be the stop sign

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:44.850
for the Russian isolation.

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:49.850
The huge tragedy is people dying today.

00:19:50.760 --> 00:19:55.760
And for Russia, the tragedy is not only

00:19:55.950 --> 00:19:59.310
what's happening now, but also this,

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:03.300
the kind of situation that Russia is,

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:05.670
has ended up in already.

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:07.830
- There are no winners in war.

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:11.190
Like everything, I agree that I too hope

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:12.540
that the freedom will win,

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:17.190
that something good will
come out out of this,

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.210
like in the future.

00:20:18.210 --> 00:20:20.910
But I think these are the consequences

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:22.860
not the winners of the war.

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:24.720
- People will be dead.

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:26.790
You cannot get them back.

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:28.350
Economies will be destroyed.

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:33.350
And okay, in the long run later,

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:35.342
we will have a winner.

00:20:35.342 --> 00:20:36.853
We will rebuild etc,

00:20:39.507 --> 00:20:44.507
but the damage war, any
war causes is too big.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:48.090
- I would like to add
that all Russian people

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:52.320
that I met here have
very healthy thoughts.

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:56.051
- I think for Russian person
will call this all propaganda.

00:20:56.051 --> 00:20:57.212
(Veronika chuckles)

00:20:57.212 --> 00:20:58.690
Ukrainian propaganda.

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:00.713
- Yeah, I think we're
all on the same side.

00:21:00.713 --> 00:21:05.034
- They will also say that we
are getting paid by America.

00:21:05.034 --> 00:21:05.910
- Yeah.

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:06.743
- Yeah

00:21:06.743 --> 00:21:07.680
- Thousands and thousands dollars.

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:08.513
- Yes.

00:21:08.513 --> 00:21:10.480
- Yeah, We basically say the same (beep).

